With \code{keep_alive = TRUE} (the default), closing the tip parks the bound output in a hidden holder instead of
destroying it, so reopening the tip shows it at once without recomputing unless its reactive inputs changed. When a
parked output is shown again, hovercraft refreshes its visibility and size state so suspended outputs update.
With \code{keep_alive = FALSE}, closing the tip unbinds and removes the output from the page, and the next open builds it
again.

While the output computes (including async renders), hovercraft shows a plain loading placeholder unless the output
already uses an external loader. \code{shinycssloaders} is tested; \code{waiter} and \code{bones} are expected to work but are
untested. If the render errors, the tip shows the error with a Retry button. If the output returns \code{NULL} or empty
